    "notes": "Owner-FCF series = reported FCF - SBC (interest income not stripped; net debt). FY2020->FY2025 owner FCF 2,164 -> 2,293 (+1.2%/yr) and FY2022->FY2025 1,013 -> 2,293 (+31%/yr) are both artefacts: FY2022 trough (Meritor acquisition working capital), FY2024 279 (EPA settlement ~1.9bn). SBC is ~0.3% of revenue so owner and reported CAGRs barely differ. Revenue 5yr CAGR includes the Meritor acquisition (Aug-2022) and the 2024 Atmus split-off (removes filtration revenue from FY2024 on). Equity 5yr CAGR 9.0% sits within 30% of revenue (11.2%) and EPS (11.3%), so no divergence flag. EPS FY2023 (5.19, EPA settlement charge) and FY2024 (28.55, Atmus split-off gain) are distorted; the endpoints used are not."
  },
  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Power Systems keeps compounding on hyperscale/AI standby and prime power (generators, natural-gas gensets, BESS) while Distribution/aftermarket grows with the installed base. North American heavy-duty truck gets a modest EPA-2027 pre-buy in FY2027 and pays for it with a FY2028 air pocket; China on/off-highway recovers slowly. Accelera losses shrink after the electrolyzer exit. Revenue lands at ~44bn by 2030 (just short of the 45-50bn target) and EBITDA settles at a mid-cycle ~19% (company basis), not the >20% management targets.",
    "bull": "Data-center power demand stays structural through the decade and the large-engine capacity expansion fills; the EPA-2027 rule holds and triggers a full pre-buy, with HELM/X10 content gains; the post-pre-buy dip is shallow because Power Systems and aftermarket carry the mix. Cummins hits the top of its raised 2030 targets (~49bn revenue, >20% EBITDA) and buybacks continue.",
    "bear": "Hyperscaler capex digests after 2027 and Power Systems backlog normalises, just as the EPA-2027 NOx rule is delayed or diluted -- no pre-buy, and a freight recession plus Section 232 tariffs push FY2028 NA truck and construction volumes down ~10% with operating deleverage to ~14.5% EBITDA. PACCAR/OEM in-sourcing erodes engine share; margins recover only to ~16%, roughly the pre-data-center mid-cycle."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Cyclical industrial valued on unlevered owner FCF built from components, with the truck cycle (pre-buy then air pocket) explicit in every scenario and mid-cycle terminal margins capped at 12-15x terminal FCF. Risk is charged in the flows and scenario weights, not stacked in the discount rate. SBC is immaterial (~0.3% of revenue), so the house/street band is narrow.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Hyperscaler/AI data-center capex slowdown hitting the highest-margin segment (Power Systems)",
      "EPA 2027 NOx rule delay/reversal removing the pre-buy",
      "North American freight/construction downturn and Section 232 tariffs",
      "OEM engine in-sourcing (PACCAR) and customer concentration",
      "Retained JV earnings (China/India) not converting to cash; NCI valued at a multiple, not book",
      "Warranty exposure on new HELM/X10 platforms (accrual 2.8bn)"
    ]
  },
