    "notes": "Model: owner-FCF component DCF with cyclical adaptations (routing row: US cyclical industrial). Cummins is an operating manufacturer/distributor whose value is its free cash flow; no bank/REIT/holdco features. Cyclicality handled in the FLOWS: FY2026 guidance year (revenue +10-13%, company EBITDA 18.0-18.5%) followed by an EPA-2027 pre-buy in FY2027 and a truck-demand air pocket in FY2028 in every scenario, with terminal margins set at a mid-cycle level rather than the FY2026-27 peak, and a 12-15x terminal cap. FY0 = FY2025 (revenue 33,670). Reported FY2025 FCF 2,386; FY2024 FCF 279 was depressed by the ~1.9bn EPA emissions settlement payment and FY2022 by Meritor integration working capital, so the FCF CAGRs are noise. FY2025 net income includes 458m of Accelera electrolyzer charges (415m non-cash). Base year-1 owner-FCF margin ~9% vs TTM reported FCF of ~3.4bn (8.9% of TTM revenue) plus after-tax interest -- consistent. No filings extracted to text (XBRL-only ticker); anchors from SEC companyfacts and Metrics.csv.",
